<Base
  title="About Save My Gig — Built by a DJ Who's Been There"
  description="Save My Gig is a free emergency tool for DJs, built from 35+ years inside the electronic music industry."
  path="/about"
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="status-line">About</div>

    <h1 style="margin-bottom:1rem">BUILT BY A DJ<br /><span class="accent">WHO'S BEEN THERE</span></h1>
    <div class="review-flag">DRAFT — Antonio to review/personalize the story.</div>

    <p>Save My Gig exists because of one specific feeling: standing in a booth, crowd waiting, and a CDJ that refuses to read your USB. If you've felt it, you know. If you haven't yet — you will, and this site will be here.</p>

    <p>I'm <strong>Antonio Afonso</strong>. I've spent more than 35 years inside the electronic music industry — including as International Managing Director of <strong>Green Valley</strong>, working with <strong>DJ Mag</strong>, and managing artists. I've watched the best DJs in the world handle disasters, and I've watched talented DJs lose nights they didn't have to lose.</p>

    <p>This site is free, has no account, and sells you nothing while you're in trouble. The emergency flow is a clean tunnel: no ads, no upsells, just the fastest route back to playing. If it saves your night and you want to give something back, there's a book and a coffee button — after you're safe, never before.</p>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">The Booth Bible</h3>
      <p class="dim">The full field manual behind this site, endorsed by Eduardo Philipp, Richard Zijlma, Akio Ide and Carl Heath.</p>
      <a href="/bible" class="btn btn-neutral" data-event="book_click" data-placement="about">📖 See the book</a>
    </div>

    <p class="dim" style="text-align:center;margin-top:2rem">
      Questions, feedback, war stories: <a href="mailto:savemygig@gmail.com">savemygig@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
